From: Keith Packard <keithp@keithp.com>
Date: Tue, 30 Jul 2019 16:46:05 -0700
Subject: Add snek mode

Snek is a small Python subset which runs on a variety of embedded
controllers. It currently supports the ATmega328p, ATmega32U4, SAMD21G
and SiFive FE310-G000 processors with ports to a range of boards that
include those processors.

Signed-off-by: Keith Packard <keithp@keithp.com>

---

v2:
	Fix snek 'put' tests

	This test was attempting to open a real device; if that failed,
	the test would fail. Fixed to bypass the actual device open while
	still testing the function behavior.

	Close serial port on quit

	Make sure we clean up any lock files or other serial state
	when the program terminates with an active serial connection.

	Make sure snek repl is running before trying 'get' operation

	This makes sure the serial link is ready to go.

	Add more snek usb IDs

v3:
	Add USB ID for SiFive HiFive1 revb board

	Leave 'get' text pane untitled and unmodified

		Leaving the pane untitled means the user will be
		prompted for a name when saving, instead of
		overwriting some existing 'snek.py' file.

		Resetting the buffer to unmodified reflects the fact
		that the code is saved on the target Snek device.

	Warn if 'get' target pane is modified. This avoids
	smashing modified code.

v4:
	Add USB ID for Arduino SA Nano 33 IoT board

v5:
	Add USB ID for Duemilanove
	Add USB ID for Arduino Mega 2560
	Enable SW flow control on Snek boards

v6:
	Allow serial ports to be opened at different baud rates

		This adds an optional baud rate parameter to
		open_serial_link and uses that instead of always using
		115200.  This handles the Arduino Mega 2560 board running
		snek at 38400 baud.

v7:
	Ensure 'put' snek script ends with newline. This avoids
	parse errors when loading the script on the target

v8:
	Reformat with black

v9:
	Wait for input from duemilanove devices that
	get rebooted when the serial connection starts.

v10:
	Rebase to current master, adapt to new REPLConnection class

v11:
	Handle empty text for 'put' operation. Thanks to @devdanzin
	for catching this bug!

v12:
	Rebase to current development version, adapt to Snek version
	1.6 flow control, which uses ENQ/ACK

v13:
	Adapt to snek version 1.7 which supports many more boards.

Signed-off-by: Keith Packard <keithp@keithp.com>
